    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 2nd with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Trea Turner** (78.64) and **Kyle Schwarber** (77.46). Both benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Randy V\u00e1squez, whose 4.75 xERA allows our top bats to exploit positive park factors and high-leverage lineup positions. **Yordan Alvarez** (74.26) remains a set-it-and-forget-it play; despite a neutral park environment, his elite 0.454 xwOBA against Bubba Chandler\u2019s 4.27 xERA makes him the safest bet for run production. Meanwhile, **Caleb Durbin** (60.48) offers a unique strategic advantage today; while his score is modest, his high contact rate and the slow delivery of Shane Baz suggest a prime opportunity to chase the scarcest category on our board: stolen bases.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical risks today, most notably with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (51.03) and **Christian Yelich** (54.83). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** faces a difficult platoon disadvantage against Gage Jump, compounded by unfavorable wind conditions, which caps his upside despite his elite sprint speed. **Christian Yelich**, conversely, is staring down a tough assignment against Trevor McDonald; while his dynamic platoon edge keeps him playable, the 2.97 xERA of the opposing arm significantly suppresses his efficiency score. Consequently, **Colt Keith** (44.50) was the primary casualty on our bench; while he remained in the conversation, his poor platoon split (L/L) against Steven Matz ultimately led the optimizer to prioritize the higher-upside profiles of **Junior Caminero** and **Dillon Dingler**. With several lineups still pending, we must remain vigilant for late-scratch news, particularly regarding the primary spots for **Carson Benge** and **Luke Raley**, as any shift out of their projected batting orders could necessitate a rapid re-evaluation of their projected efficiency.",
